# Consumer-owned schema extension (issue 13 — API Tokens). The raw
# createAPIToken / updateAPIToken / deleteAPIToken CRUD is subtracted in
# sqlgen.yml: an API Token's secret is server-owned, so a client must never set
# its token_hash, user_id, or expiry directly. These blessed mutations are the
# safe surface — they mint the secret server-side, hash it, stamp the owner, and
# return the plaintext exactly once (it is never stored and never readable again),
# mirroring how inviteToWorkspace (issue 04) owns the invitation token.
#
# Not admin-guarded: creating a token is member self-service — a User mints one to
# act on their own behalf (story 13) or to run automation (story 14), authorized
# by identity + Active Workspace alone (api_tokens is absent from the authz
# guarded tables). Revocation is authorized inside the resolver instead: the
# owner of a personal token, or a Workspace owner/admin, may revoke it (story 15).
#
# Resolver bodies live in api_token.resolvers.go and are preserved across
# `sqlgen generate` by gqlgen's copy-through semantics.

"""
The result of minting an API Token. The secret is returned exactly once, at
creation — it is stored only as a hash and can never be retrieved again.
"""
type CreateAPITokenResult {
  "The created API Token (metadata only — the secret it authenticates with is never stored in plaintext)."
  apiToken: APIToken!
  "The plaintext token secret, shown exactly once. Store it now; it cannot be recovered."
  secret: String!
}

"""
Details for minting an API Token in the caller's Active Workspace. Only the
label, optional scopes, and optional expiry are client-controlled; the secret,
its hash, the owning User (for a personal token), and the Workspace are all set
server-side.
"""
input CreateAPITokenInput {
  "Human-readable label for the token."
  name: String!
  "Granted permission scopes (recorded; enforcement is out of scope per the PRD). Omit for none."
  scopes: [String!]
  "Optional expiry; omit for a token that never expires."
  expiresAt: Time
}

extend type Mutation {
  """
  Mint a personal API Token in the Active Workspace, owned by the caller, so a
  service or script can call the API on their behalf (PRD story 13). Any member
  may create one for themselves. Returns the token metadata and the plaintext
  secret, shown exactly once.
  """
  createAPIToken(input: CreateAPITokenInput!): CreateAPITokenResult!

  """
  Mint a service (userless) API Token in the Active Workspace so automation can
  authenticate without a personal account (PRD story 14). The token carries no
  owning User; a request presenting it acts in the Workspace with baseline member
  access. Returns the token metadata and the plaintext secret, shown exactly once.
  """
  createServiceAPIToken(input: CreateAPITokenInput!): CreateAPITokenResult!

  """
  Revoke an API Token in the Active Workspace so it can no longer authenticate
  (PRD story 15). The caller must own the token (a personal token) or hold an
  owner/admin Role in the Workspace. Idempotent in effect — the token row is
  deleted. Returns true on success.
  """
  revokeAPIToken(id: UUID!): Boolean!
}
